window.docContents[244].resolve({"/External-Cross-References/Dybk___r-___--An-Ontology-on-Property/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--External-Cross-References--Dybk___r-___--An-Ontology-on-Property":{"contents":"Indexed by Dybkær section, with the term as printed and this work's corresponding\ndeclaration.\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009External Cross-References","header":"30.1. Dybkær —  An Ontology on Property","id":"/External-Cross-References/Dybk___r-___--An-Ontology-on-Property/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--External-Cross-References--Dybk___r-___--An-Ontology-on-Property"},"/Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy/Mechanization___-what-a-dimension-index-still-cannot-separate/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy--Mechanization___-what-a-dimension-index-still-cannot-separate":{"contents":"The other line is mechanization, and its strongest prior result is a formalization of\nthe ISQ and the SI in a proof assistant\n: a quantity carries\nits dimension as a type index, so dimensionally incoherent arithmetic is rejected by the\ntype checker rather than deferred to a run-time check.\n\nThat is a real calculus, and it is one this work carries too — as , the forgetful\nfunctor of point 5 of the next subsection, whose job is to certify. What it is not is a kind layer.\nIndexing on the dimension collapses the fibers of : volumetric and gravimetric\nwater content, relative permittivity and reflectivity, torque and energy each share an\nindex and are therefore one type, so the distinction a kind-of-property exists to draw\ncannot be stated there, let alone enforced. Neither do the axes that hang off a kind\nrather than off a dimension follow from it — the scale that decides which operators are\ndefined, the interaction algebra, the dedicated kind, the aggregation laws. Dimensional\ncoherence remains necessary; it was never sufficient.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Why a calculus, not a taxonomy","header":"3.4. Mechanization: what a dimension index still cannot separate","id":"/Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy/Mechanization___-what-a-dimension-index-still-cannot-separate/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy--Mechanization___-what-a-dimension-index-still-cannot-separate"},"/Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy/What-a-description-logic-cannot-express/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy--What-a-description-logic-cannot-express":{"contents":"A description logic captures the taxonomy but is structurally unable to capture\nthe calculus. The recurring gap is arithmetic, operations,\ndefinedness-conditions, laws, and proofs:\n\n* Dimension arithmetic (): OWL2 has no\n  datatype arithmetic; in Lean it is an ordinary function with a homomorphism\n  theorem.* The interaction algebra (torque  angle  energy): role chains\n  are binary, regular, and carry no arithmetic side-conditions; in Lean it is a\n  ternary relation with a dimensional-coherence proof obligation.* Scale-type operator gating (which of  are defined): DL has\n  no operations; in Lean the scale indexes which typeclasses apply, and\n  monotonicity of availability is a proved meta-theorem.* Extensivity ():\n  no quantified arithmetic in DL; in Lean it is a -theorem.* Units (a unit is a chosen value of a kind; conversion is a ratio): no\n  arithmetic in DL; in Lean it is a definition with a round-trip theorem.* Meta-theorems (specialization is a preorder;  is a homomorphism): a\n  DL reasoner checks consistency, not laws — proving the laws is the point.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Why a calculus, not a taxonomy","header":"3.2. What a description logic cannot express","id":"/Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy/What-a-description-logic-cannot-express/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Why-a-calculus___-not-a-taxonomy--What-a-description-logic-cannot-express"}});